{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And Moses went up.</b> Above it says נגד ההר, and the meaning here is: and Moses went up to the mountain of Elohim." "And the meaning of ויקרא אליו השם — HaShem had already called him, for without permission he would not have gone up." "And it says מן ההר, because he did not go up above the mountain, for there HaShem spoke with him. And do not find it difficult because afterward it says, וירד ה' על הר סיני (below, verse 20), for this is stated in reference to all Israel, that they saw the cloud and the fire, as it is written, ודבריו שמעת מתוך האש (Deuteronomy 4:36)." "And the meaning of לאמר — for He called him to say: כה תאמר לבית. And the meaning is a comprehensive statement: לבית יעקב — those who are present today and their children after them." "And ותגיד לבני ישראל — these are the elders, and they will tell all the people. And so it is written, ויבא משה ויקרא לזקני העם (verse 7), and after that it is written, ויענו כל העם יחדו (verse 8)." "And the word בית I have already explained."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:35:48.745995608Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}